==English==

===Etymology===
Maybe from {{etyl|fr}} {{term|lang=fr|bigot}} "a bigot, hypocrite" from {{etyl|frm}} {{term|bigot|lang=frm}}, from {{etyl|fro}} {{term|lang=fro|bigot}}, a derogatory term applied to Normans for their frequent note of the {{etyl|ang}} oath {{term|bi God|bī God!|lang=ang}} "by God". (More at {{l|en|by}}, {{l|en|God}}), or maybe from {{etyl|es}} {{term|bigote||moustache}}. <ref>{{R:Online Etymology Dictionary}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈbɪɡət/}}, {{SAMPA|/"bIg@t/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# one who is obstinately or [[intolerant]]ly devoted to his or her own opinions and [[prejudice]]s
# one who is strongly [[partial]] to one's own [[group]], [[religion]], [[race]], or [[politics]] and is [[intolerant]] of those who differ.

====Derived terms====
* [[bigoted]]
* [[bigotry]]

===See also===
* [[holier-than-thou]]
* [[hypocrite]]

